  "notes": "All geometry must conservatively enclose the ACTUAL robot, hand, tool, cables and complete scene within the measured workspace. Eight link radii enclose base/joint1/.../joint7/TCP segments. Self-exclusion indices and distal payload contact masks require actual field review. Capsule/box checks are conservative envelope checks, not inferred whole-body meshes. Unknown/empty geometry cannot authorize motion. Only payload-vs-named fixture contact in the measured insertion region can be exempted; robot-vs-fixture checks remain active. TCP corridors need measured enclosing radius and complete path review. 5N/1Nm are the native fixed stop thresholds, not certified insertion control. Every measurement needs real evidence. Real RGB-D observations and all installed parts are bound per phase; no simulator paths or scene identities are accepted. Held-only views require a fresh basket scene_observations packet by default. The alternative requires named measured static boxes enclosing every unseen loose object. The enforced native 0.02rad tracking-error budget is included in collision inflation and may conservatively reject tight insertion paths; no smaller unimplemented threshold is assumed. A tighter joint_tracking_error_limit_rad is accepted only with actual measured stop-test evidence and must be enforced by the native dynamic runner; it can never exceed 0.02rad. Measured ring-shell capsules_part_m may conservatively preserve real holes; solid cylinder/capsule fallback will reject some narrow ring/pin paths.",
